# Mint auxiliary backing

This is outside the checks. The prior laboratory's read-only clean image is
`C1/base/mint.qcow2` (the actual location differs from the task's `install/`
shorthand). It remains the direct immutable backing of a new access overlay.
The old image is never modified.

`../reuse-base.py mint` creates an overlay, uses the preserved serial login once,
and applies `access.sh`: install/enable OpenSSH, add the lab public key, and permit
noninteractive sudo. The final transport is SSH. The driver pins the old image's
direct path with `qemu-img rebase -u` before changing the registry link, makes the
new overlay read-only, tests a fresh clone, and destroys the disposable clone.

Status-only execution records are saved in `raw/mint/status.json`: initial
serial access setup, SSH exit 37, root exit 0, shutdown, fresh-clone boot and exit
37, and destruction all succeeded. Elapsed: 2026-11-23T06:24:36Z–06:25:32Z
(56 seconds). No failed step occurred.
